<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brahmanabad</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brahmanabad was an ancient city in lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, whose ruins lie near Shahdadpur in Sanghar District. It was a provincial centre of the Brahman dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tashkent">Chach</a> and Dahir, and was taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-qasim">Muhammad ibn Qasim</a> during the Arab conquest of Sindh in 712. The Arab capital of Mansura was founded nearby.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brahmanabad.jpg" alt="Brahmanabad" width="284" height="276" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wasimawan at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coins_Amirs_of_sindh.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
